# SRG-APP-000840-WSR-000210  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, update the list of
# passwords when organizational passwords are suspected to have been
# compromised directly or indirectly.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000840-WSR-000210
group:           V-264347
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004060
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None, and the web tier adds nothing: Splunk Web authenticates through
                 authentication.conf, the product holds no password deny list to update,
                 and no setting represents a suspected compromise event.

external:        Detection and declaration of suspected compromise and the resulting list
                 update - carried by the organization's incident response procedure.
external:        Holding and updating the list that screens web-tier logins - carried by
                 the directory service or identity provider, or by a proxy fronting Splunk
                 Web.

manual_reason:   No conf key expresses the list or a compromise event, so no observed
                 configuration value can decide this requirement.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437-600;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16
finding:         Not a finding against the application: the product holds no password deny
                 list for the web tier and has no setting representing suspected
                 compromise, so this requirement is carried by the organization's incident
                 response procedure and the identity provider; this determination is from
                 the perspective of the application layer alone.
